{"Device limit enforcement uses COUNT then a separate INSERT/UPDATE without transactional protection, allowing concurrent requests to observe count < limit and insert, exceeding the configured device limit": 0.9306215643882751, "When the device limit is reached, anonymous authentication returns a raw sentinel error (not errutil), which is handled by the middleware as a generic 401/redirect, making the user/admin experience unclear and hard to distinguish from other auth failures": 0.7763943672180176, "updateDevice treats RowsAffected()==0 as 'device limit reached', but some DBs can return 0 even when a row matched but no effective change occurred (e.g., timestamp precision truncation), which can incorrectly deny an existing device when the limit is reached": 0.5969061255455017, "Anonymous.Authenticate now calls TagDevice synchronously using the request context, and TagDevice can execute DB work (COUNT + INSERT/UPDATE) on cache misses, coupling request authentication latency/reliability to the anon_device DB path without an explicit timeout bound": 0.9375353455543518}